{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Shoham stones, etc.</b> One needs to know why He wrote <b>shoham stones and setting stones</b> in order after all the eleven kinds, when it would have been fitting to arrange them before gold and silver, for they are superior to them. Perhaps it is because we find that the princes brought them last, when they saw that Israel had brought everything needed for the Tabernacle, and you will find that they said, may their memory be for blessing (Bemidbar Rabbah ch. 12), that HaShem was displeased by this and deducted one letter from them — ״וְהַנְּשִׂיאִם״ is written (without the יו״ד). Therefore HaShem arranged them last, to indicate that they are below all of them, and because of the very reason that they are last. Understand this." "<b>Further,</b> it appears fitting to say based on what they said in Yoma, chapter Ba Lo (Yoma 69a), that priestly garments are permitted to derive benefit from, which implies that sacrificial misappropriation (me'ilah) does not apply to them. And I subsequently saw that the Rambam wrote likewise in chapter 5 of the Laws of Me'ilah. According to this, priestly garments are not on a par with the vessels of the Tabernacle and its service, all of which have a sanctity superior to that of priestly garments and are subject to sacrificial misappropriation. From this it is just to arrange shoham stones and setting stones last after all the eleven items, since all eleven items are necessities of the Tabernacle and its service, whereas the stones are only for priestly garments. And even though among the eleven items there are also some that serve the needs of priestly garments, nevertheless there is not a single kind among the eleven that does not include necessities of the Tabernacle and its service — whereas the stones are exclusively for priestly garments." "Further, it appears based on their words, may their memory be for blessing, who said in Yoma (Yoma 75a) that the clouds brought the shoham stones, etc. — if so, they were brought from a high source without toil or exertion and without cost. Necessarily, then, He arranged their offering after all the offerings that are brought from one's pocket and through toil."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:17.513239998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}